## Why This Is Asked

This question tests integration of privacy-preserving computation with hardware-assisted trust, and designs that scale across untrusted fog nodes while preserving tenant isolation.

## Key Concepts

- Threshold cryptography
- Trusted Execution Environments
- Secure aggregation
- Provenance and replay protection
- Cross-tenant isolation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal handler sketch for /cca_score/tt_share
async function handleShare(req){
  const {tenant_id, device_id, t_of_n, shard, attestation, nonce} = req.body;
  if(!verifyAttestation(attestation, device_id)) throw new Error("Bad attestation");
  // store share and nonce for later aggregation
  await storeShare(tenant_id, device_id, t_of_n, shard, nonce);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle stragglers and missing shares in the t-of-n scheme?
- What are the security trade-offs of using TEEs vs. pure MPC for this use case?
